      {
        "native_id": "1zmpx8lhv62z",
        "status": "resolved",
        "body": "On November 3, 2026, between 12:34 and 13:51 UTC, some users experienced authentication failures and errors with the REST and GraphQL APIs, pull requests, Issues, and GitHub Copilot. On average, the error rate was 0.46% and peaked at 0.98% of API requests. Copilot API errors averaged 2.0% and peaked at 3.1%.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis was caused by a bug in our process for replacing control-plane servers in one of our compute clusters. When a replacement server did not receive a timely response from the existing cluster, it incorrectly created a separate cluster. This stopped traffic from reaching much of the cluster's capacity and overloaded the authentication servers that were still handling requests.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWe mitigated the incident by removing the incorrectly configured server.\u003cbr /\u003eWe are also fixing the replacement logic and adding safeguards to prevent servers in this state from serving traffic.",
        "created_at": "2026-11-03T13:56:18.729Z"
      }
    ],
    "first_seen_at": "0001-01-01T00:00:00Z",
